<Ui>
    <!--
        WHAT IS LEFT OF THIS FILE, AND WHY IT STILL EXISTS (decision 1841).

        The four templates this file used to build — `OptionFrameBoxTemplate`,
        `OptionsButtonTemplate`, `OptionsCheckButtonTemplate` and `OptionsSliderTemplate` — now come
        off the player's chain out of `Interface\FrameXML\OptionsFrameTemplates.xml`, which the
        manifest lists directly above this entry. Our transcription of them is gone.

        **The same basename appears twice in benilla.toc on purpose.** A bare name is a file we
        ship, a path is the reference's own (the manifest's rule since 1751), so the two entries are
        unambiguous to the loader even though they read alike to a person. This one loads second and
        adds exactly one name the chain's file does not have.

        THAT NAME IS `UIOptionsCheckButtonTemplate`, and its home in the reference is
        `UIOptionsFrame.xml` — a file we do not build at all, because benilla's own options window
        is `OptionsFrame.xml`, a different design. So the template has no chain file to arrive from
        and would simply vanish if this file did.

        It is not ours and not invented: it is in `reference/1.12-globals.tsv`, and the corpus names
        it at 8 `CreateFrame` call sites — the nameplate addons build their whole options panel out
        of it. `panel_template_tests.rs` is the driver that says so.

        WHEN THIS FILE GOES: the day `UIOptionsFrame.xml` migrates. The template comes from there,
        this file has nothing left, and the manifest loses a line.

        WHAT THE SWAP GAVE BACK. Our version factored the two widgets' hover into one
        `BenillaOptionsWidget_ShowTooltip` helper, on the reasoning that "two copies of one
        behaviour is how they end up disagreeing". The reference open-codes it inline in each
        template's `<OnEnter>`, identically, and that is what runs now — the helper is gone with the
        rest, and nothing else called it.
    -->

    <!-- ref UIOptionsFrame.xml l.6-10: a 26x26 override of the chain's own
         `OptionsCheckButtonTemplate`, which it inherits from. -->
    <CheckButton name="UIOptionsCheckButtonTemplate" inherits="OptionsCheckButtonTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="26" y="26"/></Size>
    </CheckButton>
</Ui>
